course: dictionary
lesson: 8710
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. The word senior is a good example. It can mean older, higher in rank, or for adults.
explain: «Senior citizen» is the official term for an old person, often over 60 or 65. Here senior means older. Check it: «old citizen» would fit, so senior means older in this phrase.
explain: «The Church of England is led by bishops, with the Archbishop of Canterbury as senior bishop.» Here senior means higher in rank. The Archbishop is above the other bishops, so he is in charge of them.
explain: «She is my senior by two years» is different again. It means she is older than me. When senior is used to compare two people, it means the older one.
fact: Senior can mean older, higher in rank, or for adults, depending on the sentence.
fact: As a noun, «senior» means a person who is older than another: «She is my senior by two years.»
fact: «Senior citizen» is an official term for an old person, often over 60 or 65.
fact: In the UK, senior school is another name for a secondary school.
fact: In the US and Canada, a senior is a student in the final year of high school or university.
exercise: Advertisers use «senior discount» because it sounds nicer than «old people's discount». What does senior mean here? | A student in the last year | *Older | Higher in rank | Very tall
exercise: «The senior manager will see you now.» What does senior mean in this sentence? | A student in the final year | *Higher in rank or position | Older than you | Sad and tired
exercise: «The senior team won the match.» In sport, what does senior mean? | Players who are very young | Players who wear red shirts | *For adults, at the top level | Players who are very quiet
test: «Three years my senior» means the other person is | the same age as me | in a different school | *older than me by three years | younger than me
test: «Senior», as in «John Smith Sr», means | *the father with the same name as his son | the youngest child in a family | a person in charge of a bank | a student in the final year
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The cinema has a senior discount for tickets»? | Final-year students | For children under 10 | *For older people | Higher in rank
